===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|riban}}, {{m|enm|ryban}}, {{m|enm|ryband}}, from {{der|en|fro|riban}}, {{m|fro|ruban}} ( > modern {{cog|fr|ruban}}), of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Likely from a {{der|en|gem}} compound whose second element is cognate with {{cog|en|band}}. Compare {{cog|dum|ringhband|t=necklace|lit=ring-band}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɪbən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ribbon.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪbən|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A long, narrow strip of material used for decoration of clothing or the hair or gift wrapping.
# An [[awareness ribbon]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Time|author=Olivia B. Waxman|title=Wearing a Pink '''Ribbon''' for Breast Cancer Awareness? Here's How Awareness '''Ribbons''' Became a Thing|date=Oct 1 2018
|passage=With Monday marking the beginning of October’s annual Breast Cancer Awareness Month observance, supporters will be donning their pink '''ribbons''' as a show of support for ongoing research for a cure.
|url=https://time.com/5408929/awareness-ribbons-history/}}
# An [[inked]] strip of material against which type is pressed to print letters in a [[typewriter]] or [[printer]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2018|author=Mark J. P. Wolf|title=The Routledge Companion to Media Technology and Obsolescence
|passage=They were single-shift, frontstroke, typebar typewriters with four-bank QWERTY keyboards, inked by a '''ribbon'''.}}
# A narrow strip or shred.
#: {{ux|en|a steel or magnesium '''ribbon'''}}
#: {{ux|en|sails torn to '''ribbons'''}}
## {{lb|en|cooking}} In [[ice cream]] and similar [[confection]]s, an ingredient (often [[chocolate]], [[butterscotch]], [[caramel]], or [[fudge]]) added in a long narrow strip.
# {{lb|en|shipbuilding}} {{alternative form of|en|ribband}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A painted [[moulding]] on the side of a ship.
# A [[watchspring]].
# A [[bandsaw]].
# {{lb|en|slang|dated|in the plural}} Reins for a horse.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1887|author=James Inglis|title=Our New Zealand Cousins
|passage="Here, sir, hold the '''ribbons'''." This to me, throwing me the reins. Jack got down from his perch, and after a little search in the bush was rewarded by the capture of the poor dazed pigeon, who was consigned to safe custody in the boot.}}
# {{lb|en|heraldry}} A [[bearing]] similar to the [[bend]], but only one [[eighth]] as wide.
# {{lb|en|spinning}} A [[sliver]].
# {{lb|en|journalism}} A [[subheadline]] presented above its parent [[headline]].
# {{lb|en|computing|graphical user interface}} A [[toolbar]] that incorporates [[tab]]s and [[menu]]s.

